Janis Papanagnou wrote:

>>> "floating wand wresting trick"
>> 
>> This is also called "lev-wresting". Levitate, adjust the wand you 
>> want to wrest to slot "E", then just keep "E" pressed until you get
>> the "You wrest one last charge from the worn-out wand.--More--"
>> prompt. This is a 0-turn action, i.e. it does NOT consume ANY
>> turns. It can be used to safely wrest a wand of wishing on Astral,
>> for example.
> 
> I was under the impression that this works without levitation as 
> well; start the engrave command but abort the command (don't write 
> anything). Yes, I just confirmed in explore mode; engrave-aborting a
> charged wand will cost a turn, the same with an empty wand will not
> cost a turn as long as no wish is granted. Once the wish is released
> it costs again a turn.

Yes, that works, too.

Engraving while levitating as described has the advantage that it is
both faster (in real time) and much less error-prone, since you can just
keep "E" pressed until you get the wrest prompt.

To give you an idea... I lev-wrested dozens of wands of wishing in my
last extinctionist game (stthX on NAO). Sometimes it took more than 20
seconds to get the wrest prompt :D. I don't even want to know how long
that would have taken manually.


